Description: refuse a full open pull request page instead of trusting stack discovery
Author: Azhou AI Hub
Forwarded: no

`gh pr list` returns a page with no signal saying whether it was cut short, and
it returns the newest pull requests first. A repository with a full page of open
pull requests therefore handed stack discovery a list that had silently dropped
an older pull request from the bottom of the stack, so the ordering named the
wrong parent and the watcher drove the stack in the wrong order. A page as long
as OPEN_PR_LIMIT is now a query error rather than a topology.

